{"event_type":"review","id":"d0c54457fc9eb202e32d2808c7e51f44f5eb9a8874e4e3c4ccf069fac8e313ec","occurred_at":"2026-11-20T10:17:17Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f3be958a94c54c2e378d7e863027984f6608b5e8a53f790436581a24e7c34412","sha256":"f3be958a94c54c2e378d7e863027984f6608b5e8a53f790436581a24e7c34412"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0263ee1018f3f87e5e4a0ce9d388258c3c2ad52a6bcb89cf61764c333ae3035c","sha256":"0263ee1018f3f87e5e4a0ce9d388258c3c2ad52a6bcb89cf61764c333ae3035c"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/29b8f372e2ccb0ec0bf414224539b59d1dd2d0a8dce189fd32341793a263a62d","sha256":"29b8f372e2ccb0ec0bf414224539b59d1dd2d0a8dce189fd32341793a263a62d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45adb6966e7f0fc78e2960bd357aed9a1cb2c0eea1750285001f41dee870d175","sha256":"45adb6966e7f0fc78e2960bd357aed9a1cb2c0eea1750285001f41dee870d175"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c63f65846af2a29147ca145a6a933337dcc9eb5c72885c16ebdb361a02ea57bd","sha256":"c63f65846af2a29147ca145a6a933337dcc9eb5c72885c16ebdb361a02ea57bd"}],"attempt_id":"e27bfb88a9ef4f568e25b7835a682b428fc35b903ec2c1021af460d2e3f2394c:0:1","base":"59820f73a4b7446bd1dd02d1f731db9d84554b09","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f1557bdfc36b0e0ec4e8089efe548f4bfa16f6d8","body":"**Check sibling preservation in the active queue.**\n\n`apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py:110` reads the dictionary captured before preparation. If preparation replaces `old-run` with a stale record, both assertions still pass against the detached dictionary. Read `old-run` from `self.queue` after preparation, then check that it is queued and still contains F2. This accepts a valid replacement without missing a stale one.","id":"d74469245876ceca8f280403b1718ac1b21db2c52cf195edf2039fdb2001f1b6","intervals":[[110,111]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check sibling preservation in the active queue."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"f1557bdfc36b0e0ec4e8089efe548f4bfa16f6d8","body":"**Check the retained sibling decision after replay.**\n\n`apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py:560` checks only that the row remains `needs-human`. A second event with a distinct ID and the same action would leave that status unchanged and pass the test. After the first replay, assert that the outbox retains exactly one decision for the sibling. After the second replay, assert that it retains the same decision and no additional one.","id":"ce0ee5c34383243a85111bab9394902271c0f0896770d39d770ae30d7383d560","intervals":[[560,560]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Check the retained sibling decision after replay."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","body":"**Keep the job query successful in the unsettled-job case.**\n\nThis replacement sets `settled=False` but also drops `query_ok=True` and `rc=0`. A check that ignores `settled` and rejects missing query evidence still passes at Line 1012. Keep the successful query fields and supply the running job. That isolates the unsettled state from the failed-query case already tested at Line 886.","id":"0d091658bafc4c26a37922f5e6782e49a2b25b8f6b42253949f08a84048b8897","intervals":[[1000,1001]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep the job query successful in the unsettled-job case."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","body":"**Make the stale checksum match the downloaded bytes.**\n\nAt Line 172, both the stale and refreshed checksums differ from `b\"unexpected\"`. If the fetch skips the refresh and verifies against the stale checksum, it still raises `ValueError` and leaves no final image. Write `vm.sha256_bytes(b\"unexpected\")` to the stale manifest and keep the refreshed checksum different. The test will then fail if the fetch uses the stale checksum.","id":"5e2439f8ad28decf0386e930d9f8119e87b9c23e3a22f71bb09c9da7350b6f10","intervals":[[171,172]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Make the stale checksum match the downloaded bytes."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","body":"**Disable commit signing for the fixture.**\n\nIf a developer has `commit.gpgSign=true` but no available signing key, the fixture commit fails before `verify_source_scripts` runs. `--no-verify` bypasses hooks; it does not disable signing. Add `--no-gpg-sign` at Line 537 so the test still creates a real commit without requiring developer credentials. ([git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-commit.html?utm_source=openai))","id":"f4cd4b7898de0eaf36b33234c8d4bcf7839b593fef7b787cc7e333aeba67da8c","intervals":[[537,537]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Disable commit signing for the fixture."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","body":"**Test each post-boundary refusal independently.**\n\nThis fixture makes direct activation succeed after manager restart and dependency activation succeed after reboot. Because Line 1097 checks one combined result, `build_checks` could ignore either boundary and the test would still pass. Start each case with both boundaries valid, then change one return code and require `mask_persisted=False` for that case.","id":"3c2b4481588929e630d2f816436d4953067a7559180a55af025780c1c9964a88","intervals":[[1087,1092]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Test each post-boundary refusal independently."}],"head":"f361ed9bcf4529cc4e061d46505b75475c2e0cae","head_tree":"7bd3609e0990306a32150fc9478915937c36e1ec","input_scope":[{"blob":"4300eb598999bb348f601d4941a2c1e90fe890a9","intervals":[[1,1089]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_unit_switch.py"},{"blob":"f1557bdfc36b0e0ec4e8089efe548f4bfa16f6d8","intervals":[[1,890]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py"},{"blob":"8e6510c7ed6d76f148aa4f863bc5f9df6da0dbc8","intervals":[[1,796]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_review_admission_execution.py"},{"blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","intervals":[[1,1207]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py"}],"job_id":"e27bfb88a9ef4f568e25b7835a682b428fc35b903ec2c1021af460d2e3f2394c:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"4300eb598999bb348f601d4941a2c1e90fe890a9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_unit_switch.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"f1557bdfc36b0e0ec4e8089efe548f4bfa16f6d8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_bounded.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"8e6510c7ed6d76f148aa4f863bc5f9df6da0dbc8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_review_admission_execution.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"5d3c12102373923ac3a2a53a61e76af29414e866","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_vm_feasibility.py","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"4300eb598999bb348f601d4941a2c1e9